\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Come, holy celestial Dove,
\par To visit a sorrowful breast,
\par My burden of guilt to remove,
\par And bring me assurance and rest!
\par Thou only hast power to relieve
\par A sinner o'erwhelmed with his load,
\par The sense of acceptance to give,
\par And sprinkle his heart with the blood.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. With me if of old Thou hast strove,
\par And strangely withheld from my sin,
\par And tried, by the lure of Thy love,
\par My worthless affections to win;
\par The work of Thy mercy revive,
\par Thy uttermost mercy exert,
\par And kindly continue to strive,
\par And hold, till I yield Thee my heart.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Thy call if I ever have known,
\par And sighed from myself to get free,
\par And groaned the unspeakable groan,
\par And longed to be happy in Thee;
\par Fulfill the imperfect desire,
\par Thy peace to my conscience reveal,
\par The sense of Thy favour inspire,
\par And give me my pardon to feel.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. If when I had put Thee to grief,
\par And madly to folly returned,
\par Thy pity hath been my relief,
\par And lifted me up as I mourned;
\par Most pitiful Spirit of grace,
\par Relieve me again, and restore,
\par My spirit in holiness raise,
\par To fall and to suffer no more.\tab\tab 
\par                                Amen.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

